                <pb facs="0335" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg321"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Monthly Historical Report of the United States Army Group of AMAG, for
                    August, states that the Group “began its actual supply of the Greek armed forces
                    when, on 2 August 1947, the first American ship arrived at Piraeus with a
                    military general cargo, vehicles and rations. Following in the wake of this
                    vessel during August were ten additional American ships with military supplies
                    and equipment.” (868.20 Missions/9–2647) For the Department’s statement of
                    August 22 on early aspects of aid to Greece, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 31, 1947, page 428.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
